pytest-services: isolate test locks on Darwin builders

Darwin build sandboxes share /tmp. The default memory_root_dir fixture
uses /tmp/service-locks, whose port and display files can belong to another
Nix build user. This fails pytest-services and its CherryPy/Poetry dependents.

Override the fixture only in the package's own tests, using pytest's private
temporary directory. Keep the port and display allocation tests enabled.
The fixture override is enabled only on Darwin.

Local fix; no upstream issue filed.

--- a/pkgs/development/python-modules/pytest-services/default.nix
+++ b/pkgs/development/python-modules/pytest-services/default.nix
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 {
   lib,
+  stdenv,
   buildPythonPackage,
   fetchFromGitHub,
   psutil,
@@ -52,6 +53,16 @@
 
   pythonImportsCheck = [ "pytest_services" ];
 
+  preCheck = lib.optionalString stdenv.hostPlatform.isDarwin ''
+    # Darwin sandboxes share /tmp with other Nix build users.
+    cat >> tests/conftest.py <<'PY'
+
+    @pytest.fixture(scope="session")
+    def memory_root_dir(tmp_path_factory):
+        return str(tmp_path_factory.mktemp("pytest-services"))
+    PY
+  '';
+
   disabledTests = [
     # Tests require binaries and additional parts
     "test_memcached"
